---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms & Privacy | Silver Lining of Hope"
  description="Terms of use and privacy practices for silverliningofhope.com, including how we handle case information, tips, and donor data."
  heading="Terms & privacy"
  intro="Short version: we protect the people we serve, and we don't sell anything about you."
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Terms & privacy', href: '/terms' }]}
>
  <div class="container--narrow section prose">
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This site is operated by Silver Lining of Hope, Inc, an Indiana
      501(c)(3) nonprofit (EIN 39-2169099). Contact us any time via the
      <a href="/about/contact">contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Case information</strong> shared with us is treated as confidential and shared only with the family involved and, where appropriate, law enforcement.</li>
      <li><strong>Anonymous tips</strong> are exactly that: the <a href="/get-help/submit-a-tip">tip form</a> has no required identity fields and we do not log IP addresses from tip submissions.</li>
      <li><strong>Contact and volunteer information</strong> is used only to respond to you and coordinate our work. We never sell or rent personal information.</li>
      <li><strong>Donations</strong> are processed by our third-party donation processor; we receive your name and gift amount for receipting, governed by that processor's privacy policy.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Not legal or emergency services</h2>
    <p>
      We provide research and advocacy, not legal advice, and we are not an
      emergency service. If someone is in immediate danger, call 911. Content
      on this site is general information, not a substitute for advice from
      an attorney or guidance from law enforcement.
    </p>

    <h2>Content and cases</h2>
    <p>
      We publish case-related information only with family consent or from
      public records, and we correct errors promptly —
      <a href="/about/contact">tell us</a> if you find one. Please don't
      reuse victims' photos or case materials from this site without
      permission.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
